{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4585","published":"2026-10-29T09:03:15Z","modified":"2026-10-29T09:15:35.994687023Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-93834"],"summary":"qemu security update","details":"QEMU is a FAST! processor emulator using dynamic translation to achieve good emulation speed.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA use-after-free vulnerability was found in QEMU&apos;s 9pfs subsystem. A race condition between the main thread and a worker thread when processing concurrent Tlcreate and Twalk requests allows a malicious guest user to craft a fid path containing stale heap data, bypassing directory traversal restrictions and escaping the shared directory boundary. This can lead to arbitrary host file read/write and code execution (VM escape) as the QEMU process user.(CVE-2026-93834)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qemu","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qemu&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qemu-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-curl-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-iscsi-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-rbd-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-ssh-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debuginfo-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debugsource-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-guest-agent-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-hw-usb-host-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-img-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-aarch64-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-arm-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-riscv-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-x86_64-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-binfmt-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-static-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["qemu-help-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["qemu-8.2.0-63.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["qemu-8.2